{
  "title": "Infinite carousel on a phone: the arrows glide across the seam both ways, and a real finger wraps around",
  "description": "Infinite estrategia-web/carousel on /prueba-carrusel-bucle/ on a 402 px touch phone: «Carrusel con una de más» and «Carrusel en bucle» cross the seam each way with the arrows plus one ordinary step, each trip recorded and checked like on desktop (it glides); a real finger (the touch customStep: start, a move per frame, still six frames, lift — measured 03-10-2026: a synthesized scroll gesture moves nothing, moves without a frame between do not finish the gesture, and a finger that lifts while moving starts a fling that never ends) dragging right on the first slide shows the last one and dragging left goes on, with scroll-snap, on the block carousel and on the Query one. Read by browser-carousel-infinite-phone. It was carousel-infinite.test.mjs (section 6, level 3) until 29-10-2026.",
  "writes": true,
  "timeout": 15000,
  "initScripts": [
    "modules/carousel/tests/browser/probes.js"
  ],
